<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puerto Cortés</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puerto Cortés is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast of north-western Honduras and the country's main seaport. Its deep natural harbour developed from the late nineteenth century as the terminus of the national railway and an outlet for banana exports, and it is linked to the industrial centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-pedro-sula">San Pedro Sula</a>, about 60 kilometres to the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puerto-cortes.jpg" alt="Puerto Cortés" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dennis Garcia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Malecon_Puerto_Cortes_Honduras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
